// SOFTMAX activation with acc_scale=1 (no identity-matmul pass-through).
//
// IMPORTANT: pinned to TVM's actual compiled literal (6.06016e-05), not the
// full-precision Python value (6.0601649051e-05). codegen.cc streams this
// `double` through a plain `ostringstream <<`, whose default precision() is
// 6 significant digits, so that's what TVM's own gemmini_out/lib0.c actually
// emits (verified directly against that file). qc = c/(a*bert_scale^2) is
// hypersensitive to bert_scale (inverse-square), and with this bert_scale
// magnitude qc is ~2.6e8, small enough that sum_exp already overflows int32
// when accumulated over a full 81-wide softmax row -- so which *specific*
// garbage value it wraps to depends on bert_scale's exact bits. Matching
// TVM's truncated literal exactly (rather than the "more correct"
// full-precision value) is what reproduces TVM's actual measured output.
#define NLB_MATMUL_BERT_SCALE 6.06016e-05f

